WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.001 size:81% position:41% line:92%
-This is a true story.

00:00:01.001 --> 00:00:02.802 align:start size:94% position:6%
Well, not -- it's inspired by
a true story.

00:00:02.802 --> 00:00:05.071
I don't know if these guys were
actually --

00:00:05.071 --> 00:00:06.239 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Word for word.
-Word for word?

00:00:06.239 --> 00:00:08.942
-This is actually a documentary.
-This is a documentary.

00:00:08.942 --> 00:00:10.643 align:start size:94% position:6%
But these are friends,
a group of friends

00:00:10.643 --> 00:00:13.246
who have been playing
a real game of Tag for 30 years.

00:00:13.246 --> 00:00:13.813 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah, it's true.

00:00:13.813 --> 00:00:17.384
There was a "Wall Street
Journal" profile on these guys.

00:00:17.384 --> 00:00:20.153 align:start size:94% position:6%
They're from
Spokane, Washington.

00:00:20.153 --> 00:00:24.357 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Audience cheers ]

00:00:24.357 --> 00:00:25.058 size:75% position:38% line:92%
There is 10 of them.

00:00:25.058 --> 00:00:27.794 align:start size:94% position:6%
We scaled it down
for narrative reasons to five.

00:00:27.794 --> 00:00:28.962 line:92%
-Yeah. And it's cash, right?

00:00:28.962 --> 00:00:31.064 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Right, right.
We couldn't afford it.

00:00:31.064 --> 00:00:32.832 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, right. Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:32.832 --> 00:00:34.567 align:start size:94% position:6%
-But they really do play
this game.

00:00:34.567 --> 00:00:36.436 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it's actually kind of
a beautiful thing

00:00:36.436 --> 00:00:39.906
because it's kept them together
as friends for 30 years.

00:00:39.906 --> 00:00:42.208
You know, when you get older --
-Yeah.

00:00:42.208 --> 00:00:45.145
-...it's harder to stay in touch
with people.

00:00:45.145 --> 00:00:46.746 line:92%
We have Facebook and stuff now.

00:00:46.746 --> 00:00:48.681 align:start size:94% position:6%
But to actually be
in the same place,

00:00:48.681 --> 00:00:52.619
this game does that for them
and it's a beautiful thing.

00:00:52.619 --> 00:00:53.486 line:92%
-It is a beautiful thing.

00:00:53.486 --> 00:00:56.222 align:start size:94% position:6%
I still think it would be
a hard sell if I told my wife

00:00:56.222 --> 00:00:58.491 align:start size:94% position:6%
I got to -- it's Tag time.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:58.491 --> 00:01:01.428 align:start size:94% position:6%
No matter how many years I've
been doing it, I think --

00:01:01.428 --> 00:01:03.797 align:start size:94% position:6%
-"Sorry, honey,
you got the kids tonight.

00:01:03.797 --> 00:01:05.198 line:92%
I got to go run around and tag."

00:01:05.198 --> 00:01:06.633 align:start size:94% position:6%
-"I got my tag thing."
-Yeah.

00:01:06.633 --> 00:01:09.069 align:start size:94% position:6%
Well, it is only one month
out of the year.

00:01:09.069 --> 00:01:10.203 line:92%
-Well that's -- I guess she --

00:01:10.203 --> 00:01:12.238 size:75% position:38%
She would definitely
give me that, yeah.

00:01:12.238 --> 00:01:14.340 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So it's reasonable. Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:14.340 --> 00:01:16.076 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Jeremy Renner is one of
your cast mates.

00:01:16.076 --> 00:01:18.812
And one of your other cast
mates, Annabelle Wallis was here

00:01:18.812 --> 00:01:20.747 align:start size:94% position:6%
talking about how he broke
both his arms.

00:01:20.747 --> 00:01:23.016
-Right.
-She was not one of the taggers.

00:01:23.016 --> 00:01:23.650 align:start size:94% position:6%
You are.
-Yeah.

00:01:23.650 --> 00:01:25.318 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Did you get hurt?
Any injuries for you?

00:01:25.318 --> 00:01:26.920 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No, I didn't.
I didn't get hurt at all.

00:01:26.920 --> 00:01:33.827 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it's worth, I think,
pointing out that Jason Bourne

00:01:33.827 --> 00:01:35.829 align:start size:94% position:6%
and the guy
from "Mission: Impossible"

00:01:35.829 --> 00:01:39.132 align:start size:94% position:6%
and Hawkeye the Avenger
got hurt.

00:01:39.132 --> 00:01:40.433 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:40.433 --> 00:01:41.034 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-And I did not.

00:01:41.034 --> 00:01:43.770 size:81% position:41%
-You came out -- yeah.
-I came out unscathed.

00:01:43.770 --> 00:01:44.504 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:44.504 --> 00:01:47.740
-Well, do you think -- do you
think the industry has noticed?

00:01:47.740 --> 00:01:51.411
-Well, that's what's so weird is
that now there is all this buzz.

00:01:51.411 --> 00:01:53.980
'Cause everyone was like,
"Helms got out scot-free,

00:01:53.980 --> 00:01:58.151
without a scratch, so like maybe
he's the next big action star."

00:01:58.151 --> 00:01:59.185 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, wow.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:59.185 --> 00:02:01.921
And it's like --
I'm just hearing all this buzz.

00:02:01.921 --> 00:02:04.991 align:start size:94% position:6%
I don't know where it started.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:04.991 --> 00:02:05.558 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I don't know.

00:02:05.558 --> 00:02:07.861 align:start size:94% position:6%
-But this is a palpable buzz
in Hollywood?

00:02:07.861 --> 00:02:09.229 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Palpable buzz, Seth.
-Wow.

00:02:09.229 --> 00:02:13.066 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Seth, it's -- I mean, this
is -- it's buzzing.

00:02:13.066 --> 00:02:13.600 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah, yeah.

00:02:13.600 --> 00:02:15.635 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Everyone is like,
"He's gonna be --"

00:02:15.635 --> 00:02:19.139
And this is -- I mean,
I'm very humbled by this.

00:02:19.139 --> 00:02:19.939 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
There's Oscar buzz.

00:02:19.939 --> 00:02:22.275 align:start size:94% position:6%
-There's Oscar buzz too?
-Yeah, for me.

00:02:22.275 --> 00:02:25.678
Yeah, and I, again, I don't know
where it started.

00:02:25.678 --> 00:02:26.713 align:start size:94% position:6%
I don't know.
-Wow.

00:02:26.713 --> 00:02:30.383
Is it the Oscar for not getting
hurt on the set?

00:02:30.383 --> 00:02:30.917 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:30.917 --> 00:02:33.786 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It's because I just --
I transformed in this role.

00:02:33.786 --> 00:02:36.890 align:start size:94% position:6%
-All right.
So here's my question though.

00:02:36.890 --> 00:02:37.624 size:75% position:38% line:92%
So Renner's Hawkeye.

00:02:37.624 --> 00:02:41.361
If Ed Helms is now the new
action star, superhero guy,

00:02:41.361 --> 00:02:43.863 align:start size:94% position:6%
what would be a good superhero
for you?

00:02:43.863 --> 00:02:45.765 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So I've been thinking
about that.

00:02:45.765 --> 00:02:50.036
When I do get the call from
Marvel, what am I gonna say?

00:02:50.036 --> 00:02:50.670 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:50.670 --> 00:02:53.306 line:92%
And I think a good one would be,

00:02:53.306 --> 00:02:56.543 align:start size:94% position:6%
because Renner's Hawkeye,
I could be Hawkguy.

00:02:56.543 --> 00:02:57.243 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Okay.
-Yeah.

00:02:57.243 --> 00:03:00.213
-Seems very similar.
-No. It's not. It's not at all.

00:03:00.213 --> 00:03:03.082
Because Renner runs around with
a bow and arrow.

00:03:03.082 --> 00:03:06.419 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I'm just the guy who knows
a lot about hawks.

00:03:06.419 --> 00:03:08.454 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, okay.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:08.454 --> 00:03:08.888 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:03:08.888 --> 00:03:12.258
Hawkguy, he's like your go-to
guy for hawk-related trivia.

00:03:12.258 --> 00:03:12.959 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Gotcha. Facts.

00:03:12.959 --> 00:03:14.661 align:start size:94% position:6%
-A lot of people
don't know this.

00:03:14.661 --> 00:03:16.930 align:start size:94% position:6%
Falcons and hawks
get confused a lot.

00:03:16.930 --> 00:03:17.597 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Gotcha.
-Right?

00:03:17.597 --> 00:03:19.899 align:start size:94% position:6%
But Hawkguy can tell you
the difference.

00:03:19.899 --> 00:03:20.867 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Gotcha.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:20.867 --> 00:03:22.502 align:start size:94% position:6%
Could he tell me
a lot about falcons

00:03:22.502 --> 00:03:25.071
or would he push me off
to someone else for that?

00:03:25.071 --> 00:03:27.207 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, he'd push you off
to Falconguy.

00:03:27.207 --> 00:03:29.042 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Right, exactly.
-Obviously.

00:03:29.042 --> 00:03:29.576 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:29.576 --> 00:03:31.110 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Not to be confused with
the falcon.

00:03:31.110 --> 00:03:33.413
-Jon Hamm is gonna be Falconguy.
-Yeah.

00:03:33.413 --> 00:03:34.981 size:78% position:39% line:92%
-And I'll be Hawkguy.

00:03:34.981 --> 00:03:35.548 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-That's great.

00:03:35.548 --> 00:03:38.351 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think your scenes
will be the best in that film.

00:03:38.351 --> 00:03:41.955
-It's just like I said -- don't
know where the buzz started.

00:03:41.955 --> 00:03:42.589 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:42.589 --> 00:03:43.323 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
So humbled by it.

00:03:43.323 --> 00:03:44.324 size:88% position:44% line:92%
-So humbled by the buzz.

00:03:44.324 --> 00:03:45.124 line:92%
-But we'll see what happens.

00:03:45.124 --> 00:03:47.627 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You shot in Atlanta,
which is where you are from.

00:03:47.627 --> 00:03:49.295 align:start size:94% position:6%
-My hometown, yeah.
Atlanta, Georgia.

00:03:49.295 --> 00:03:51.864 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So how was that?
Was it nice to be back home?

00:03:51.864 --> 00:03:52.432 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-It's awesome.

00:03:52.432 --> 00:03:55.702 line:92%
I do -- I love going back home.

00:03:55.702 --> 00:03:59.806 size:81% position:41%
It, you know, stirs up
a lot of old memories,

00:03:59.806 --> 00:04:02.141 line:92%
old jobs and school and stuff.

00:04:02.141 --> 00:04:05.311 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Where were -- What was young
Ed Helms doing for jobs?

00:04:05.311 --> 00:04:07.347 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, I worked --
I was a lifeguard.

00:04:07.347 --> 00:04:08.314 align:start size:94% position:6%
-All right.
-At a pool.

00:04:08.314 --> 00:04:10.883 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, that's where they do it.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:10.883 --> 00:04:11.517 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Well, it's funny.

00:04:11.517 --> 00:04:13.253 align:start size:94% position:6%
When you say
that you were a lifeguard,

00:04:13.253 --> 00:04:16.122 align:start size:94% position:6%
people are like,
"Whoa, that's impressive."

00:04:16.122 --> 00:04:17.490 size:78% position:39% line:92%
I was not impressive.

00:04:17.490 --> 00:04:17.924 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Okay.

00:04:17.924 --> 00:04:18.958 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I was a lifeguard
at a city pool.

00:04:18.958 --> 00:04:21.461 align:start size:94% position:6%
The most I did, like, the most
heroic thing I did

00:04:21.461 --> 00:04:24.097
was stopped children from peeing
in the pool.

00:04:24.097 --> 00:04:25.465 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:25.465 --> 00:04:26.032 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-And that's --

00:04:26.032 --> 00:04:28.001 align:start size:94% position:6%
-If you are stopping them from
peeing in the pool,

00:04:28.001 --> 00:04:30.737 align:start size:94% position:6%
that means they're doing it
from outside the pool?

00:04:30.737 --> 00:04:33.106 align:start size:94% position:6%
'Cause otherwise how --
[ Laughter ]

00:04:33.106 --> 00:04:33.740 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
How can you tell?

00:04:33.740 --> 00:04:35.441 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No, you can tell.
-You can?

00:04:35.441 --> 00:04:36.209 line:92%
-You can absolutely tell.

00:04:36.209 --> 00:04:38.645 align:start size:94% position:6%
Because they can be
in the middle of, like,

00:04:38.645 --> 00:04:42.282
a crazy game of Marco Polo,
and when they start to pee,

00:04:42.282 --> 00:04:44.350 align:start size:94% position:6%
they just drift away.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:44.350 --> 00:04:46.986 align:start size:94% position:6%
And they get this blank look
on their face.

00:04:46.986 --> 00:04:52.358
And it's just -- they're like...
[ Laughter ]

00:04:52.358 --> 00:04:57.363 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:57.363 --> 00:04:59.565 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It strikes me that
once you see that face,

00:04:59.565 --> 00:05:01.167 align:start size:94% position:6%
it's already too late.
-It's too late.

00:05:01.167 --> 00:05:04.570
But you can shame them into
hopefully not doing it again.

00:05:04.570 --> 00:05:05.738 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I see. I gotcha.
-Right?

00:05:05.738 --> 00:05:07.840 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So you're policing
the next time out?

00:05:07.840 --> 00:05:09.309 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I'm a child shamer.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:09.309 --> 00:05:12.378
-That's really what a lifeguard
was, a child shamer.

00:05:12.378 --> 00:05:14.113 line:92%
-Let's go back to Oscar buzz.

00:05:14.113 --> 00:05:14.647 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:05:14.647 --> 00:05:16.649 align:start size:94% position:6%
Because again,
somebody keeps saying it.

00:05:16.649 --> 00:05:17.517 line:92%
Somebody keeps repeating it.

00:05:17.517 --> 00:05:21.554 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, no, I've heard it a lot
in the last five minutes.

